WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.390 --> 00:00:04.060
Game of Thrones Season 6 Episode 8 – let’s
have a look.

00:00:04.060 --> 00:00:07.410
We begin in Braavos, where Lady Crane performs
that play again.

00:00:07.410 --> 00:00:11.960
She’s taken Arya’s advice and added a
bit in her speech about wanting vengeance.

00:00:11.960 --> 00:00:16.290
She heads backstage, finds a wounded Arya,
and takes her home to heal her up.

00:00:16.290 --> 00:00:18.269
Which is a big deal for Arya.

00:00:18.269 --> 00:00:22.560
You gotta remember that her life these last
few years has been one horror after another

00:00:22.560 --> 00:00:27.980
– losing her family, imprisonment at Harrenhal,
roaming the riverlands, joining a death cult.

00:00:27.980 --> 00:00:32.489
So this situation of comfort and trust and
normalcy is a really special moment, a rare

00:00:32.489 --> 00:00:34.680
chance to rest and heal.

00:00:34.680 --> 00:00:39.220
Though, the books emphasise that Arya may
have hurts that won’t heal.

00:00:39.220 --> 00:00:43.340
In the books she says she feels a “hole
inside her where her heart had been”, that

00:00:43.340 --> 00:00:46.469
“The hole will never feel any better”.

00:00:46.469 --> 00:00:50.670
After all that she’s been through, Arya
is traumatised, deeply damaged, which makes

00:00:50.670 --> 00:00:53.230
you wonder how her story could possibly end.

00:00:53.230 --> 00:00:57.589
Like, after the fighting’s done, one way
or another, she’ll hardly marry some lord

00:00:57.589 --> 00:01:02.190
and settle down as the noble lady she never
wanted to be in the first place, will she?

00:01:02.190 --> 00:01:06.380
So it’s interesting that in this scene she
talks about travelling west of Westeros, seeing

00:01:06.380 --> 00:01:08.409
the edge of the world.

00:01:08.409 --> 00:01:10.799
Maybe that’s how her story could end.

00:01:10.799 --> 00:01:15.170
Maybe she could say her farewells, get on
a boat, and sail west, into the sunset, like

00:01:15.170 --> 00:01:20.650
Frodo in Lord of the Rings, passing on to
a place of rest somewhere between heaven and

00:01:20.650 --> 00:01:21.650
death…

00:01:21.650 --> 00:01:23.170
That could be beautiful.

00:01:23.170 --> 00:01:27.080
That said, the Arya revelations this episode
are dumb.

00:01:27.080 --> 00:01:30.420
It turns out that Arya’s stabbing wasn’t
a trick, wasn’t part of a plan, there wasn’t

00:01:30.420 --> 00:01:35.210
a twist – Arya seriously decided to go for
a haircut and have a nice afternoon stroll,

00:01:35.210 --> 00:01:39.969
unarmed, not paying attention, when she knew
a deadly assassin was hunting her.

00:01:39.969 --> 00:01:42.950
Has she learned nothing from her training
these last seasons?

00:01:42.950 --> 00:01:46.490
And her stabbing looked like it’d kill her,
but all it takes is a band-aid from Crane

00:01:46.490 --> 00:01:48.090
and she’s okay?

00:01:48.090 --> 00:01:52.730
This makes the stabbing feel like a cheap
trick on the audience, a shock to spark the

00:01:52.730 --> 00:01:53.730
clickbait.

00:01:53.730 --> 00:01:57.950
Game of Thrones is meant to be a show where
if you fuck up, there are lasting consequences.

00:01:57.950 --> 00:02:02.090
So having Arya get herself stabbed from her
own carelessness, then conveniently healed

00:02:02.090 --> 00:02:06.109
in the next episode, undermines the brutal
realism that separates Thrones from other

00:02:06.109 --> 00:02:07.700
fantasy shows.

00:02:07.700 --> 00:02:11.860
Every time a character gets stabbed then comes
back the same as they were before, we care

00:02:11.860 --> 00:02:17.040
less next time a character is stabbed – and
that’s happened like three times this season

00:02:17.040 --> 00:02:18.040
already?

00:02:18.040 --> 00:02:22.730
So that’s lame, but the episode does get
better because this time, Arya has a plan.

00:02:22.730 --> 00:02:26.810
Somewhere in the riverlands, a bunch of brotherhood
dudes are talking shit when the Hound comes

00:02:26.810 --> 00:02:31.350
along and murders them all with an axe, to
avenge the death of Brother Ray and his community

00:02:31.350 --> 00:02:33.080
who were slaughtered last episode.

00:02:33.080 --> 00:02:34.880
But were these guys even guilty?

00:02:34.880 --> 00:02:38.620
Like, the older two were in the group that
threatened Ray’s village, so presumably

00:02:38.620 --> 00:02:40.420
they were involved in the massacre.

00:02:40.420 --> 00:02:44.720
But the younger guys we’ve never seen before,
they seem to be just a couple of naïve young

00:02:44.720 --> 00:02:49.269
men – so unless the Hound knows something
we don’t, he just murdered innocent people,

00:02:49.269 --> 00:02:50.269
didn’t he?

00:02:50.269 --> 00:02:52.349
Are we meant to cheer for this?

00:02:52.349 --> 00:02:56.470
Maybe this is where the character of the Hound
is going, he’s becoming more an antihero

00:02:56.470 --> 00:03:01.330
than a hero, more a Punisher than a Superman
– someone who’s willing to do terrible

00:03:01.330 --> 00:03:03.819
things in the name of justice.

00:03:03.819 --> 00:03:04.950
Which could be interesting.

00:03:04.950 --> 00:03:09.040
But it’s striking how opposite this is to
what happens to the Hound in the books, where

00:03:09.040 --> 00:03:14.210
he joins a sort of monastery to atone for
his sins, he begins a life of peace.

00:03:14.210 --> 00:03:18.360
These chapters in the book are about showing
an alternative to violence and conflict, showing

00:03:18.360 --> 00:03:20.520
that peace can be possible.

00:03:20.520 --> 00:03:23.930
The representative of this in the show is
Brother Ray, but he and his whole community

00:03:23.930 --> 00:03:28.010
are wiped out in the same episode they’re
introduced – which sends the opposite message,

00:03:28.010 --> 00:03:32.629
it suggests that peace and pacifism will just
get you killed, that the only way to survive

00:03:32.629 --> 00:03:37.610
is to perpetuate this endless cycle of violence
and vengeance and suffering.

00:03:37.610 --> 00:03:41.000
If that’s the version of Westeros the show
wants to show, then so be it – but it does

00:03:41.000 --> 00:03:46.720
feel wrong to see George Martin’s arguably
anti-war story turned into a show that sometimes

00:03:46.720 --> 00:03:49.330
celebrates indiscriminate violence.

00:03:49.330 --> 00:03:53.590
Varys and Tyrion chat about the status of
Meereen, which seems to be improving since

00:03:53.590 --> 00:03:55.120
Tyrion’s peace deal.

00:03:55.120 --> 00:03:59.120
We see a red priestess preaching about Daenerys
being the chosen one of the Lord of Light,

00:03:59.120 --> 00:04:04.190
called Azor Ahai or the prince that was promised,
which could get awkward when Dany gets to

00:04:04.190 --> 00:04:08.860
Westeros, cause there the red priest Melisandre
thinks Jon Snow is Azor Ahai.

00:04:08.860 --> 00:04:13.410
You can’t have two chosen ones… this could
be a problem.

00:04:13.410 --> 00:04:17.540
Anyway Varys is going back to Westeros, probably
to kill those guys from the end of Book 5,

00:04:17.540 --> 00:04:19.990
and he and Tyrion say a sad farewell.

00:04:19.990 --> 00:04:22.750
They seem to have a real friendship here,
which is sweet.

00:04:22.750 --> 00:04:26.660
You can see why they’d feel a connection,
they’re gotta lot in common – both very

00:04:26.660 --> 00:04:31.630
clever, capable dudes who feel outcast from
society – Tyrion for being a dwarf, and

00:04:31.630 --> 00:04:33.110
Varys for being a eunuch.

00:04:33.110 --> 00:04:37.400
They’ve fond of each other in the books,
too, but book-Varys isn’t truly Tyrion’s

00:04:37.400 --> 00:04:38.400
friend.

00:04:38.400 --> 00:04:41.610
In the books, Varys manipulates Tyrion, manipulates
everyone.

00:04:41.610 --> 00:04:46.430
He has this huge, complex conspiracy going
on with his fat friend Illyrio, with totally

00:04:46.430 --> 00:04:51.580
different goals than the Varys of the show,
his character is much more extreme and complex,

00:04:51.580 --> 00:04:55.180
which is cool, but it’s also kinda nice
to see that the show-version Varys being much

00:04:55.180 --> 00:05:00.430
more able to have to actual genuine relationships,
it's like a more human version of the Spider

00:05:00.430 --> 00:05:02.600
we know from the books.

00:05:02.600 --> 00:05:06.110
In King’s Landing, the sparrows, led by
Lancel, try to seize Cersei.

00:05:06.110 --> 00:05:10.450
It’s still crazy to see how different Lancel
is from how he started – he used to be this

00:05:10.450 --> 00:05:15.640
meek incompetent kid, a fuckbuddy for Cersei,
and now, he’s in a religious militia and

00:05:15.640 --> 00:05:17.380
she’s an enemy of the Faith.

00:05:17.380 --> 00:05:18.380
Shit changed.

00:05:18.380 --> 00:05:22.170
But anyway Cersei chooses violence – she
sends in the Mountain, who goes full Darth

00:05:22.170 --> 00:05:23.680
Vader on a sparrow.

00:05:23.680 --> 00:05:28.650
Qyburn looks on like a proud soccer mom, so
pleased to see his creation growing strong.

00:05:28.650 --> 00:05:31.130
Qyburn’s another really interesting character.

00:05:31.130 --> 00:05:34.480
When Cersei first meets him, he’s described
as looking “like some little girl’s favorite

00:05:34.480 --> 00:05:39.080
grandfather”, a “soft-spoken” man “with
warm brown eyes” – he does not look like

00:05:39.080 --> 00:05:40.370
a monster.

00:05:40.370 --> 00:05:44.460
We do hear rumours that he “does black magic”,
that he was kicked out of the Citadel for

00:05:44.460 --> 00:05:48.880
performing experiments on living men, but
it’s only when Qyburn turns the dying Mountain

00:05:48.880 --> 00:05:54.380
into the monster he is now in some mysterious
terrible process involving screaming and pain

00:05:54.380 --> 00:05:59.700
and the deaths of innocent women that we realise
this sweet old man is a some Josef Mengele

00:05:59.700 --> 00:06:00.920
motherfucker.

00:06:00.920 --> 00:06:05.620
Bad guys don’t always look like bad guys
in this story.

00:06:05.620 --> 00:06:07.800
Brienne and Pod arrive at Riverrun.

00:06:07.800 --> 00:06:11.620
While Brienne chats with Jaime, Bronn chokes
Pod, for the banter.

00:06:11.620 --> 00:06:15.020
They chat for a while and Bronn teaches Pod
to fight dirty, which you could totally see

00:06:15.020 --> 00:06:19.590
coming in handy later on – maybe Pod could
save Brienne by kicking a Bolton in the nuts

00:06:19.590 --> 00:06:20.590
or something.

00:06:20.590 --> 00:06:24.940
Meanwhile, Brienne and Jaime talk, and Jaime
plays it kinda cold at first, acting dismissive

00:06:24.940 --> 00:06:29.690
of Brienne, but he does reaffirm his gift
of Oathkeeper, that Valyrian steel sword,

00:06:29.690 --> 00:06:33.740
which is an incredibly valuable gift – remember
there’s just like a dozen of those swords

00:06:33.740 --> 00:06:38.530
known left in the world – but it’s also
very symbolic, representing Jaime’s faith

00:06:38.530 --> 00:06:40.510
in and respect for Brienne.

00:06:40.510 --> 00:06:45.250
That might be the heart of Jaime and Brienne’s
relationship, cause they both crave respect,

00:06:45.250 --> 00:06:49.690
but don’t get it from the outside world,
because Brienne is a woman trying to be a

00:06:49.690 --> 00:06:54.840
knight, and Jaime’s the Kingslayer, an oathbreaker
– they both feel looked down by everyone.

00:06:54.840 --> 00:06:58.580
But through their shared suffering, Jaime
and Brienne come to see the goodness, and

00:06:58.580 --> 00:07:03.170
the strength, and the honour in each other,
even if no one else does – and that’s

00:07:03.170 --> 00:07:07.570
why it’s so tragic that they’re stuck
on opposite sides – Jaime serves King Tommen

00:07:07.570 --> 00:07:11.500
and Lannisters, while Brienne serves Sansa
Stark, who’s an enemy of the Crown.

00:07:11.500 --> 00:07:15.990
There is a bit of a star-crossed lovers vibe
here, but whether Brienne and Jaime love each

00:07:15.990 --> 00:07:20.300
other romantically or just as friends might
not be the point – they give each other

00:07:20.300 --> 00:07:23.920
the respect they both so desperately crave.

00:07:23.920 --> 00:07:27.630
So Brienne heads into Riverrun and tries to
convince the Blackfish to give up the castle,

00:07:27.630 --> 00:07:31.990
and come help Sansa and the Starks take Winterfell,
which the book-version of Blackfish probably

00:07:31.990 --> 00:07:35.510
would have done, because the main reason he
holds Riverrun is to be his loyalty to the

00:07:35.510 --> 00:07:39.690
Starks, but show-Blackfish mostly just wants
to defend his family home, so he refuses Brienne

00:07:39.690 --> 00:07:42.470
and stays inside the castle.

00:07:42.470 --> 00:07:45.810
In King’s Landing, Cersei comes to the Great
Hall for an announcement, and she wants to

00:07:45.810 --> 00:07:50.600
stand by her son Tommen, but she’s rejected
– by her son, by her uncle Kevan, and by

00:07:50.600 --> 00:07:54.450
the ladies of court – she feels an outcast
right now.

00:07:54.450 --> 00:07:58.950
Then King Tommen gives his announcement – that
trials by combat are now banned, because they’re

00:07:58.950 --> 00:08:03.960
barbaric and unfair which is pretty true – it’s
silly that having a powerful warrior on your

00:08:03.960 --> 00:08:08.010
side can excuse you for crimes, but the real
meat here is that now Cersei can’t use the

00:08:08.010 --> 00:08:11.830
Mountain to win her trial and her innocence
– so this looks to be another clever play

00:08:11.830 --> 00:08:15.120
by the High Sparrow – outsmarting Cersei
again.

00:08:15.120 --> 00:08:19.600
But also this seems to mean that we won’t
get Cleganebowl, the big theoretical fight

00:08:19.600 --> 00:08:23.220
between Gregor and Sandor that fans have been
hyped for for years.

00:08:23.220 --> 00:08:29.630
Which in some ways is unsurprising, the theory
always was pretty light on evidence and thematic

00:08:29.630 --> 00:08:34.020
resonance, but still – why would the show
hype this fight if it’s not gonna happen?

00:08:34.020 --> 00:08:37.599
“that is one trial by combat I look forward
to watching”.

00:08:37.599 --> 00:08:41.942
We might not get Cleganebowl in the way it
was imagined, but hopefully we’ll still

00:08:41.942 --> 00:08:44.200
get something like it.

00:08:44.200 --> 00:08:48.570
Anyway so Cersei has her plan ruined, she’s
now all out of options, which means she might

00:08:48.570 --> 00:08:52.310
be about to do something drastic, something
fiery.

00:08:52.310 --> 00:08:57.500
Cause at the end of the scene, Qyburn tells
Cersei he looked into a rumour and found something

00:08:57.500 --> 00:09:01.370
big – and there are lots of hints at what
this might be.

00:09:01.370 --> 00:09:06.530
Remember the wildfire, that napalmy green
stuff, we saw buried beneath King’s Landing,

00:09:06.530 --> 00:09:09.600
that King Aerys once tried to use to burn
down the city?

00:09:09.600 --> 00:09:20.080
Remember all those times Cersei said she’d
burn cities to the ground?

00:09:20.080 --> 00:09:24.080
Remember that vision in Season 2 of King’s
Landing looking like it’d been burned?

00:09:24.080 --> 00:09:28.590
There’s lots of evidence in show and books
that Cersei will try to use wildfire to burn

00:09:28.590 --> 00:09:34.200
down King’s Landing, in an act of mad revenge
and fury against everyone who wronged her.

00:09:34.200 --> 00:09:38.400
The only thing left that might stop her from
doing this is her son Tommen, who she still

00:09:38.400 --> 00:09:43.600
loves above all else, so maybe he’ll need
to die somehow to spark Cersei’s rage and

00:09:43.600 --> 00:09:44.600
grief.

00:09:44.600 --> 00:09:48.230
In the books there is the valonquar prophecy
which suggests to some that Jaime might kill

00:09:48.230 --> 00:09:52.810
Cersei to save the city, and this shot of
a dragon over King’s Landing suggests it

00:09:52.810 --> 00:10:00.340
might be dragonfire that sets off the wildfire,
either way, it looks like the capital will

00:10:00.340 --> 00:10:02.120
burn.

00:10:02.120 --> 00:10:05.610
In Meereen, we have a second instalment of
“Tyrion tries to teach Missandei and Grey

00:10:05.610 --> 00:10:09.670
Worm how to have fun”, and it goes a little
better than last time did.

00:10:09.670 --> 00:10:13.550
Tyrion makes a comment about sharing wine
with his close friends, which makes you realise

00:10:13.550 --> 00:10:16.200
– Tyrion doesn’t really have close friends.

00:10:16.200 --> 00:10:20.950
He’s in this foreign city, far from everyone
he knows, his family mostly hates him or was

00:10:20.950 --> 00:10:26.360
killed by him, his closest companions back
home were people he paid to hang around with

00:10:26.360 --> 00:10:27.360
him.

00:10:27.360 --> 00:10:30.370
Tyrion Lannister is really lonely.

00:10:30.370 --> 00:10:34.140
Their game is interrupted when the slavers
roll on in with a big fleet – looks like

00:10:34.140 --> 00:10:37.290
Tyrion’s peace deal didn’t work after
all.

00:10:37.290 --> 00:10:40.470
At Riverrun, Jaime and Edmure have an emotional
talk.

00:10:40.470 --> 00:10:44.680
We get a taste of Edmure’s suffering in
captivity these last years, and Edmure heavily

00:10:44.680 --> 00:10:49.380
criticises Jaime, asking him how he lives
with himself – giving us an example of how

00:10:49.380 --> 00:10:53.520
most people look down on Jaime – while Brienne
sees the good in him.

00:10:53.520 --> 00:10:58.400
Jaime responds by ruthlessly threatening Edmure,
saying he’ll hurl his baby son into Riverrun

00:10:58.400 --> 00:11:02.180
with a catapult, which seems to confirm Edmure’s
words that Jaime’s an asshole, but at the

00:11:02.180 --> 00:11:06.770
same time it succeeds in convincing Edmure
to give up Riverrun peacefully, so Jaime gets

00:11:06.770 --> 00:11:11.390
to keep his oath to Catelyn not to attack
Tullys, which in its own way makes Jaime an

00:11:11.390 --> 00:11:12.890
honourable man.

00:11:12.890 --> 00:11:17.130
This shot of Jaime could almost represent
this duality, with his face half in the shadow,

00:11:17.130 --> 00:11:20.170
and half in the light, somewhere between good
and evil.

00:11:20.170 --> 00:11:23.280
This is Jaime’s internal struggle.

00:11:23.280 --> 00:11:26.600
But yeah the Lannisters and Freys take Riverrun,
Brienne tries to get the Blackfish to come

00:11:26.600 --> 00:11:30.430
with her, but the Blackfish chooses to go
get himself killed offscreen instead, which

00:11:30.430 --> 00:11:34.060
is a little lame, given that the Blackfish
was talked up to be this really amazing dude,

00:11:34.060 --> 00:11:38.550
and all he ended up doing was standing around
and being grumpy, but Brienne heads off along

00:11:38.550 --> 00:11:43.920
the river and Jaime waves her goodbye, until
their paths will meet again.

00:11:43.920 --> 00:11:47.860
In Meereen, a siege begins, with the slavers
bombarding the city – the beginning of the

00:11:47.860 --> 00:11:50.300
so-called “Battle of Fire”.

00:11:50.300 --> 00:11:53.360
Just when everything’s looking terrible,
Daenerys arrives on dragonback to see what

00:11:53.360 --> 00:11:57.510
the kids have been up to while she’s been
gone and she doesn’t look pleased.

00:11:57.510 --> 00:12:01.390
So presumably, Dany will use her three dragons
to burn the slavers’ fleet, though the other

00:12:01.390 --> 00:12:05.420
thing to consider is that the ironborn are
still on their way, with their fleet.

00:12:05.420 --> 00:12:10.810
So we’ve got dragons and harpies and squids
all coming together in this crazy huge Battle

00:12:10.810 --> 00:12:12.900
of Fire.

00:12:12.900 --> 00:12:16.310
Back in the riverlands, the Hound comes across
the leaders of the brotherhood without banners,

00:12:16.310 --> 00:12:20.290
Beric Dondarrion, and Thoros of Myr, who are
about to hang Lem and some other brothers

00:12:20.290 --> 00:12:23.460
who apparently perpetrated the massacre of
Ray’s village.

00:12:23.460 --> 00:12:27.180
The Hound haggles with the brotherhood over
who gets to do the killing and how, which

00:12:27.180 --> 00:12:28.180
is… perverse.

00:12:28.180 --> 00:12:30.850
And then then they sit and have a fireside
chat.

00:12:30.850 --> 00:12:35.800
Beric and Thoros ask the Hound to join them,
offering him redemption and a purpose.

00:12:35.800 --> 00:12:39.440
They talk about winter, and the north, and
it sounds like they wanna go help fight the

00:12:39.440 --> 00:12:44.590
white walkers, which is cool – it’s not
clear how they know about white walkers, maybe

00:12:44.590 --> 00:12:46.500
Thoros saw it in his flames.

00:12:46.500 --> 00:12:49.620
Thoros, if you remember, is a red priest,
like Melisandre.

00:12:49.620 --> 00:12:53.920
He’s got a pretty cool backstory himself,
check out the Thoros video if you’re keen.

00:12:53.920 --> 00:12:58.060
But yeah looks like the Hound is going north
with the brotherhood – Beric and Thoros’

00:12:58.060 --> 00:13:01.770
flaming swords would certainly be handy against
the wights and walkers.

00:13:01.770 --> 00:13:05.580
Maybe they’ll also get involved in the Battle
of the Bastards next episode.

00:13:05.580 --> 00:13:10.540
Maybe Beric will meet Jon – they’d have
plenty to talk about, seeing as both of them

00:13:10.540 --> 00:13:13.680
were resurrected with the power of the Red
God.

00:13:13.680 --> 00:13:16.370
So lots of interesting new material to look
forward to here.

00:13:16.370 --> 00:13:21.290
In Braavos, Arya wakes to find the waif’s
killed Crane – which Arya shoulda seen coming,

00:13:21.290 --> 00:13:22.290
right?

00:13:22.290 --> 00:13:26.090
The waif gives a Bond villain bad guy speech,
because she’s a rubbish assassin, and Ayra

00:13:26.090 --> 00:13:29.260
runs away, leading the waif on a chase across
the city.

00:13:29.260 --> 00:13:33.270
Arya lures the waif to a dark room, where
she draws Needle, turns out the light, and

00:13:33.270 --> 00:13:36.190
kills the waif using her skills from her time
training blind.

00:13:36.190 --> 00:13:41.339
Which is a pretty cool plan – Arya adapted
to overcome an enemy stronger than herself.

00:13:41.339 --> 00:13:45.270
Then Arya takes the waif’s face into the
House of `Black and White, and confronts Jaqen

00:13:45.270 --> 00:13:50.690
H’ghar, who, strangely, says she is now
no one – which is weird, cause being no

00:13:50.690 --> 00:13:56.070
one is meant to mean giving up your identity
and personality, which Arya clearly hasn’t

00:13:56.070 --> 00:13:57.070
done.

00:13:57.070 --> 00:13:59.970
Maybe Jaqen’s just trying to talk his way
out of being killed here – he has got a

00:13:59.970 --> 00:14:03.550
sword to his chest – though even as Arya
leaves, he smiles for her, he’s clearly

00:14:03.550 --> 00:14:07.650
fond of her, which is like, fine, power of
friendship yay, but what’s the point of

00:14:07.650 --> 00:14:12.460
being a hardened fanatical death-worshipping
cultist who gives up their very humanity if

00:14:12.460 --> 00:14:16.230
you’re gonna just be cool with some kid
breaking all your rules and killing your other

00:14:16.230 --> 00:14:18.490
student, because you’re fond of her.

00:14:18.490 --> 00:14:23.090
The Men invested so much training in her,
and now they’re just letting her go?

00:14:23.090 --> 00:14:28.320
The Faceless Men of the show simply make much
sense, which is a real shame, but regardless

00:14:28.320 --> 00:14:32.770
we’ve now gotten to the point of the Braavos
arc – Arya is now stronger, and she’s

00:14:32.770 --> 00:14:37.210
embracing her identity as Arya Stark of Winterfell,
she says she’s going home.

00:14:37.210 --> 00:14:39.210
But what’s she gonna do there?

00:14:39.210 --> 00:14:43.769
Presumably, she’s after the people on her
list, and Walder Frey seems the obvious target

00:14:43.769 --> 00:14:47.540
– he’s been set up as a bad guy this season,
and we’ve seen him celebrating with some

00:14:47.540 --> 00:14:52.060
Lannisters in the trailers, so maybe Arya’ll
crash the party and kill Walder.

00:14:52.060 --> 00:14:57.040
We might also eventually get to see Arya meeting
her family again, seeing Sansa and Jon, coming

00:14:57.040 --> 00:14:58.279
back to Winterfell.

00:14:58.279 --> 00:15:03.110
This is big – Arya Stark is back.

00:15:03.110 --> 00:15:05.330
So that was a mixed episode.

00:15:05.330 --> 00:15:10.050
The Arya stuff was bad in parts, but there’s
cool stuff happening in Meereen, and King’s

00:15:10.050 --> 00:15:14.180
Landing, and the riverlands, and next episode
is the Battle of the Bastards, and after that,

00:15:14.180 --> 00:15:19.490
the season finale – just two episodes left
and they both promise to be huge.

00:15:19.490 --> 00:15:23.690
So thank you for watching, and thank you to
all Patrons supporting this channel on Patreon,

00:15:23.690 --> 00:15:27.940
including Eric Louis-Dreyfus, Todd Marcus,
Chris Cole, Eric Cascketta, Sean Kethcart,

00:15:27.940 --> 00:15:31.460
Sanschlaepfer, Rajiv Kothari, Caitlyn McKinney,
Javi Ortiz, v.c.

00:15:31.460 --> 00:15:33.690
gillyhoon, Jon, Nick and Bull.

00:15:33.690 --> 00:15:34.250
Cheers.

